            <div xml:id="d659">

                <pb facs="0850" n="762" sameAs="frus:frus1919Parisv02/pg762"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">763.72112/11040: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Sharp</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Acting Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris</hi>
                        </placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1918-12-17">December 17,
                            1918</date>.<lb/>[Received December 17—2:57 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>6336. War Trade Board [from Taylor]: No. 688. Attention McCormick. Laws of Allies
                    permit of trading with enemy subjects within area of occupation and our rules
                    should be modified to agree. Alsace, Lorraine are open as any French territory.
                    Taylor.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sharp</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
